  "configuration_id": "config_001",
  "reason": "With zero completed experiments, the highest-priority question is establishing a performance baseline against which all added complexity (multiprofile, learned encoders, image modality, fusion) can be measured. config_001 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) is the simplest, most interpretable configuration in the search space: a standard PCA dimensionality reduction on a single RNA profile with no learned encoder, no image, no aggregation, and no fusion. It serves as the 'null model' floor. Every subsequent experiment—whether it adds a learned RNA encoder (scvi/scgpt), a second profile with aggregation, an image branch, or a multimodal fusion—can be directly compared to this baseline to isolate the marginal contribution of each design choice. Starting with the minimal configuration also avoids confounding multiple design decisions at once and gives the cleanest reference point for the limited experiment budget."
}

